					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-3952294#post-3610992</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-3952294/the-engine-of-a-film-the-fine-game-of-nil#post-3610992</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 10 Oct 2017 19:23:30 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>psul</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2156983</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>The idea of &quot;killer flops&quot; stamping on a human face forever has promise, and I can get behind turning that into a critique of toxic masculinity. But I don't think this has a sharp enough edge - it's not focused enough to be really effective.</p> <p>If you put some more time into linking the two storylines - both plot-wise (perhaps Mary is the wife of one of the three researchers?) and textually (to bring home the point with more force) - I think that this could be very good indeed. It would also have a fresher message than the current one, which (as you say above) has been done to death in the canon already. As it stands, the Mary storyline feels too disconnected to have any real emotional impact.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-3952294#post-3610775</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-3952294/the-engine-of-a-film-the-fine-game-of-nil#post-3610775</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 10 Oct 2017 11:48:51 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>TL333s</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1304786</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>The bro half is solid lolFoundation, but intercutting it with this tragic tale of a woman living the worst life ever was, I think, a mistake. The incongruity is so offputting. And it gets more surreal as it goes &#8212; Tabula Rasa? sure, why not! &#8212; but I'm just not sure what I'm supposed to take away from this. No-vote.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
